title: Shared guide for Definitions 4-5
---
guide:

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="300" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.Def.4-5 diagram" src="defIII4.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_1",
        background: "0,0,100",
        title: "III.Def.4-5",
        pivot: "A",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;150,140;black;green",
            "B;point;free;150,40",
            "Acirc;circle;radius;A,B;0;0;black;random",
            "C;point;circleSlider;Acirc,40,30",
            "D;point;circleSlider;Acirc,50,200",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "AE;line;foot;A,CD",
            "E;point;last;AE",
            "F;point;circleSlider;Acirc,200,50",
            "Fcirc;circle;radius;F,CD;0;0;0;0",
            "GG';line;bichord;Acirc,Fcirc;0;0;0",
            "G;point;first;GG'",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G",
            "AH;line;foot;A,FG",
            "H;point;last;AH",
            "K;point;circleSlider;Acirc,130,200",
            "Kcirc;circle;radius;K,C,E;0;0;0;0",
            "L'L;line;bichord;Acirc,Kcirc;0;0;0",
            "L;point;last;L'L",
            "KL;line;connect;K,L",
            "AM;line;foot;A,KL",
            "M;point;last;AM"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

These definitions could have been broadened to distances from a line to an arbitrary point, but Euclid's needs only distances from a line to the center of a circle.

The perpendiculars *AE* and *AH* drawn from the center *A* to the lines *CD* and *FG* respectively are equal, so the lines *CD* and *FG* are equally distant from the center.

As the perpendicular *AM* is greater, the line *KL* is at a greater distance from the center.
